<BaseLayout title="Engine and drivetrain">
  <h1>Engine and drivetrain</h1>
  <p>The 2021 S60 range uses several versions of Volvo's 2.0-liter Drive-E four-cylinder platform. The engine badge matters: induction hardware, hybrid components, cooling, exhaust, transmission, and service procedures are not identical across T5, T6, and T8 models.</p>
  <ReferencePhoto src="https://www.volvocars.com/media/support-content/img4b4a330b573d9c4ec0a801524b07b5d5_1_--_--_VOICEpnghigh.png" variant="reference-diagram" alt="Volvo 2021 S60 engine compartment overview with numbered service-point callouts" caption="2021 S60 engine-compartment service-point illustration" credit="Volvo Cars" source="https://www.volvocars.com/uk/support/car/s60/2021/article/f3e117dc70239324c0a801513d2de23c/" license="Volvo Cars support illustration" />
  <p class="photo-disclaimer">The Volvo illustration is specific to the 2021 S60 owner's information, but Volvo notes that the layout can vary by engine and model variant.</p>
